WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:12.580
94. Dylan Thomas. Dylan Thomas is a beloved poet and writer from Wales. He is most famous

2
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:18.940
for his poetry, but he also wrote short stories and scripts for radio and television. He was

3
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:26.020
very talented, though he had a difficult life. Dylan Thomas was born in Swansea, South Wales,

4
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:33.700
on October 27, 1914. He was not a very healthy child. He had asthma and bronchitis, so he

5
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:39.900
usually preferred to read than to play. Thomas dropped out of school when he was 16 and went

6
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.580
to work as a journalist for the local newspaper. He wrote some famous poems when he was a teenager,

7
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:53.300
including, The force that through the green fuse drives the flower, and Death shall have no dominion.

8
00:00:53.300 --> 00:01:01.660
His first volume of poetry was published in 1934, when he had just turned 21. However, while he was

9
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:07.380
having great success with his writing, he also began to develop a drinking habit. This would

10
00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:15.420
be a problem all his life. In 1937, Thomas married Caitlin McNamara. They had three children together.

11
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.860
It was difficult for him to support his family. He wrote for movies for years, but the family

12
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:31.020
stayed poor. Then, in 1946, he published Deaths and Entrances. It changed their lives. After this,

13
00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:39.700
Thomas gave several successful speaking tours. In 1953, Thomas went to New York for a conference.

14
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:46.860
As usual, he drank very much. People worried about whether he would behave well or cause problems,

15
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:53.140
but it wasn't drinking that he should have worried about. Unluckily for him, the air quality in New

16
00:01:53.140 --> 00:02:00.780
York dropped suddenly. Smog filled the city. Thomas became very sick. By the time anyone noticed,

17
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:09.100
it was too late. Dylan Thomas died of pneumonia and bronchitis in a New York hospital on November 9, 1953.
